1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,591
One computer cannot build everything.

2
00:00:03,141 --> 00:00:04,648
A team has Linux builds,

3
00:00:04,648 --> 00:00:05,590
Windows builds,

4
00:00:05,590 --> 00:00:06,281
slow tests,

5
00:00:06,281 --> 00:00:08,480
and ten developers pushing at once.

6
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:10,553
If one machine does all the work,

7
00:00:10,553 --> 00:00:12,186
everybody waits in a line.

8
00:00:12,736 --> 00:00:14,809
Jenkins solves this with agents.

9
00:00:14,809 --> 00:00:16,752
The controller plans the work.

10
00:00:16,752 --> 00:00:17,594
Agents do it,

11
00:00:17,594 --> 00:00:18,760
on other machines,

12
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:19,861
at the same time.

13
00:00:20,411 --> 00:00:22,070
Today you add a real agent,

14
00:00:22,070 --> 00:00:23,544
send a real build to it,

15
00:00:23,544 --> 00:00:26,001
and learn where the files go afterwards.

16
00:00:27,551 --> 00:00:28,980
Here is what to expect.

17
00:00:34,530 --> 00:00:38,050
One: the words. Controller, agent, executor, label.

18
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:50,462
Two: where the files live. Workspace, artifacts, and the stash.

19
00:00:59,012 --> 00:01:00,283
Three: a live demo,

20
00:01:00,283 --> 00:01:02,158
in the real Jenkins screens.

21
00:01:02,158 --> 00:01:03,228
We add an agent,

22
00:01:03,228 --> 00:01:04,433
send builds to it,

23
00:01:04,433 --> 00:01:06,709
watch two builds run side by side,

24
00:01:06,709 --> 00:01:07,512
keep a file,

25
00:01:07,512 --> 00:01:09,721
and pass a file between machines.

26
00:01:20,271 --> 00:01:23,087
Four: the common mistakes, and where to find the lab.

27
00:01:23,637 --> 00:01:26,602
This is objective seven of the Jenkins domain.

28
00:01:28,652 --> 00:01:29,868
Four words to know.

29
00:01:30,418 --> 00:01:32,864
The controller is the brain of Jenkins.

30
00:01:32,864 --> 00:01:33,993
It keeps the jobs,

31
00:01:33,993 --> 00:01:34,746
the history,

32
00:01:34,746 --> 00:01:35,812
and the settings.

33
00:01:35,812 --> 00:01:37,129
It decides what runs,

34
00:01:37,129 --> 00:01:37,757
and where.

35
00:01:38,307 --> 00:01:39,960
An agent is another machine,

36
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:40,904
or another user,

37
00:01:40,904 --> 00:01:42,262
that does the building.

38
00:01:42,262 --> 00:01:44,033
It connects to the controller,

39
00:01:44,033 --> 00:01:45,155
and waits for work.

40
00:01:45,705 --> 00:01:48,440
An executor is one build slot on a machine.

41
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:52,510
An agent with two executors can run two builds at the same time.

42
00:01:53,060 --> 00:01:55,060
A label is a tag on a machine.

43
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:56,927
A pipeline asks for a label,

44
00:01:56,927 --> 00:01:58,127
for example maven,

45
00:01:58,127 --> 00:02:01,060
and Jenkins picks any machine that wears it.

46
00:02:01,610 --> 00:02:05,173
So the pipeline never names a machine. It names what it needs.

47
00:02:06,723 --> 00:02:08,430
Now, where do the files live?

48
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:10,647
Every job gets a workspace.

49
00:02:10,647 --> 00:02:11,574
It is a folder,

50
00:02:11,574 --> 00:02:13,550
on the agent that ran the build.

51
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:15,403
The code is checked out there,

52
00:02:15,403 --> 00:02:17,812
and the build writes its results there.

53
00:02:18,362 --> 00:02:23,610
A workspace is working space, not storage. It can be wiped, and it stays on one machine.

54
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:25,232
To keep a result,

55
00:02:25,232 --> 00:02:25,925
archive it.

56
00:02:25,925 --> 00:02:30,023
The archiveArtifacts step copies chosen files to the controller,

57
00:02:30,023 --> 00:02:31,474
attached to that build,

58
00:02:31,474 --> 00:02:32,672
for download later.

59
00:02:33,222 --> 00:02:35,257
To pass a file to a later stage,

60
00:02:35,257 --> 00:02:37,102
maybe on a different machine,

61
00:02:37,102 --> 00:02:38,565
use stash and unstash.

62
00:02:38,565 --> 00:02:41,682
Stash saves files for the rest of this one build.

63
00:02:41,682 --> 00:02:43,209
Un stash puts them back,

64
00:02:43,209 --> 00:02:43,782
anywhere.

65
00:02:44,332 --> 00:02:49,452
Archive is for people, and for history. Stash is for the pipeline, for the next stage.

66
00:02:51,002 --> 00:02:52,054
A real Jenkins.

67
00:02:52,054 --> 00:02:53,386
I sign in as admin.

68
00:02:53,386 --> 00:02:56,682
On the left is the Build Executor Status panel.

69
00:02:56,682 --> 00:02:58,155
There is one machine,

70
00:02:58,155 --> 00:02:59,417
the built in node,

71
00:02:59,417 --> 00:03:01,591
and its two executors are idle.

72
00:03:01,591 --> 00:03:03,695
That is the controller itself.

73
00:03:04,245 --> 00:03:05,648
Now we add an agent.

74
00:03:05,648 --> 00:03:06,700
Manage Jenkins,

75
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:07,471
then Nodes.

76
00:03:07,471 --> 00:03:08,663
Here is the list.

77
00:03:08,663 --> 00:03:10,276
Only the built in node,

78
00:03:10,276 --> 00:03:10,837
for now.

79
00:03:11,387 --> 00:03:11,529
New Node.

80
00:03:11,529 --> 00:03:11,686
I name it,

81
00:03:11,686 --> 00:03:11,937
build agent one.

82
00:03:11,937 --> 00:03:12,377
The type is Permanent Agent,

83
00:03:12,377 --> 00:03:12,707
a machine that stays.

84
00:03:12,707 --> 00:03:12,817
Create.

85
00:03:18,367 --> 00:03:18,557
Now its settings.

86
00:03:18,557 --> 00:03:19,219
The remote root directory is the folder where it will work,

87
00:03:19,219 --> 00:03:19,544
the workspaces live under it.

88
00:03:19,544 --> 00:03:19,712
The labels are,

89
00:03:19,712 --> 00:03:19,779
linux,

90
00:03:19,779 --> 00:03:19,891
and maven.

91
00:03:19,891 --> 00:03:20,160
The number of executors,

92
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:20,306
I set to two.

93
00:03:20,306 --> 00:03:21,360
The launch method is already the one we want: launch agent by connecting it to the controller.

94
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:21,573
The agent calls us,

95
00:03:21,573 --> 00:03:21,831
so no firewall problem.

96
00:03:21,831 --> 00:03:21,887
Save.

97
00:03:30,437 --> 00:03:30,768
The new node appears,

98
00:03:30,768 --> 00:03:31,036
with a red cross.

99
00:03:31,036 --> 00:03:31,398
Jenkins knows about it,

100
00:03:31,398 --> 00:03:31,918
but no machine has connected yet.

101
00:03:31,918 --> 00:03:32,044
Open it,

102
00:03:32,044 --> 00:03:33,069
and Jenkins prints the exact command to run on the other machine,

103
00:03:33,069 --> 00:03:33,289
with a secret,

104
00:03:33,289 --> 00:03:33,699
and the WebSocket option,

105
00:03:33,699 --> 00:03:34,298
so the agent uses the normal web port.

106
00:03:42,848 --> 00:03:44,070
On the other machine,

107
00:03:44,070 --> 00:03:45,409
I run that one command.

108
00:03:45,409 --> 00:03:48,726
Here the other machine is a second user on this computer,

109
00:03:48,726 --> 00:03:49,483
called agent.

110
00:03:49,483 --> 00:03:51,462
It is java dash jar agent dot jar,

111
00:03:51,462 --> 00:03:52,160
the address,

112
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:52,684
the name,

113
00:03:52,684 --> 00:03:53,557
and the secret.

114
00:04:04,107 --> 00:04:04,553
Back to the node list.

115
00:04:04,553 --> 00:04:04,999
The red cross is gone.

116
00:04:04,999 --> 00:04:05,525
Build agent one is online,

117
00:04:05,525 --> 00:04:05,910
with two executors,

118
00:04:05,910 --> 00:04:06,923
and it shows its own disk space and response time.

119
00:04:07,473 --> 00:04:08,862
Now the simplest use.

120
00:04:08,862 --> 00:04:09,853
A new Pipeline,

121
00:04:09,853 --> 00:04:10,977
named agent test.

122
00:04:10,977 --> 00:04:13,357
The script asks for the label maven.

123
00:04:13,357 --> 00:04:15,142
It prints the machine name,

124
00:04:15,142 --> 00:04:15,737
the user,

125
00:04:15,737 --> 00:04:16,729
and the folder,

126
00:04:16,729 --> 00:04:18,448
then waits twenty seconds.

127
00:04:18,448 --> 00:04:20,828
I will explain the wait in a moment.

128
00:04:24,378 --> 00:04:24,740
Save,

129
00:04:24,740 --> 00:04:25,754
and Build Now.

130
00:04:25,754 --> 00:04:26,985
Open the console.

131
00:04:26,985 --> 00:04:30,462
The first lines say: running on build agent one,

132
00:04:30,462 --> 00:04:32,345
in slash home slash agent,

133
00:04:32,345 --> 00:04:33,359
slash Jenkins,

134
00:04:33,359 --> 00:04:34,517
slash workspace,

135
00:04:34,517 --> 00:04:35,749
slash agent test.

136
00:04:36,299 --> 00:04:37,773
That is the workspace.

137
00:04:37,773 --> 00:04:39,047
It is on the agent,

138
00:04:39,047 --> 00:04:40,991
under the agent's own folder,

139
00:04:40,991 --> 00:04:42,465
not on the controller.

140
00:04:42,465 --> 00:04:43,672
The user is agent,

141
00:04:43,672 --> 00:04:44,476
not Jenkins.

142
00:04:44,476 --> 00:04:45,683
Different machine,

143
00:04:45,683 --> 00:04:46,688
different user,

144
00:04:46,688 --> 00:04:47,627
same pipeline.

145
00:04:48,177 --> 00:04:53,233
Now executors. Build Now, three times, quickly. That is the reason for the wait.

146
00:04:53,783 --> 00:04:55,540
Look at the executor panel.

147
00:04:55,540 --> 00:04:57,623
Build agent one runs two builds,

148
00:04:57,623 --> 00:04:58,991
one on each executor.

149
00:04:58,991 --> 00:05:01,269
The third build waits in the queue,

150
00:05:01,269 --> 00:05:02,636
until a slot is free.

151
00:05:03,186 --> 00:05:05,655
A queue means you need more executors,

152
00:05:05,655 --> 00:05:06,629
or more agents.

153
00:05:06,629 --> 00:05:08,319
Jenkins shows the problem,

154
00:05:08,319 --> 00:05:08,903
honestly.

155
00:05:09,453 --> 00:05:10,146
Now files.

156
00:05:10,146 --> 00:05:11,185
A new Pipeline,

157
00:05:11,185 --> 00:05:12,778
named cloud cart agent.

158
00:05:12,778 --> 00:05:15,756
This script builds cloud cart on the agent,

159
00:05:15,756 --> 00:05:16,518
with Maven.

160
00:05:16,518 --> 00:05:18,804
Then it archives the web archive,

161
00:05:18,804 --> 00:05:19,843
and stashes it.

162
00:05:23,393 --> 00:05:26,328
The second stage asks for a different machine,

163
00:05:26,328 --> 00:05:27,477
the built in node.

164
00:05:27,477 --> 00:05:28,945
It unstashes the file,

165
00:05:28,945 --> 00:05:29,775
and lists it.

166
00:05:29,775 --> 00:05:30,094
Save,

167
00:05:30,094 --> 00:05:30,987
and Build Now.

168
00:05:31,537 --> 00:05:32,748
Open the console.

169
00:05:32,748 --> 00:05:35,454
Stage one: running on build agent one.

170
00:05:35,454 --> 00:05:37,234
Maven builds the package,

171
00:05:37,234 --> 00:05:39,014
in the agent's workspace.

172
00:05:39,014 --> 00:05:39,370
Then,

173
00:05:39,370 --> 00:05:40,794
archiving artifacts,

174
00:05:40,794 --> 00:05:41,079
and,

175
00:05:41,079 --> 00:05:42,289
stashed one file.

176
00:05:42,839 --> 00:05:44,788
Stage two: running on Jenkins,

177
00:05:44,788 --> 00:05:46,738
in the controller's workspace.

178
00:05:46,738 --> 00:05:48,167
And there is the file,

179
00:05:48,167 --> 00:05:49,401
cloud cart dot war,

180
00:05:49,401 --> 00:05:51,415
arrived from the other machine.

181
00:05:51,965 --> 00:05:53,223
Now the build page.

182
00:05:53,223 --> 00:05:54,283
Under the build,

183
00:05:54,283 --> 00:05:55,474
the archived file,

184
00:05:55,474 --> 00:05:56,732
cloud cart dot war,

185
00:05:56,732 --> 00:05:57,924
ready to download.

186
00:05:57,924 --> 00:05:59,513
It stays with the build,

187
00:05:59,513 --> 00:06:01,565
even if the workspace is wiped.

188
00:06:02,115 --> 00:06:06,802
The workspaces link lists the folder on each machine that ran this build.

189
00:06:06,802 --> 00:06:07,893
One on the agent,

190
00:06:07,893 --> 00:06:09,306
one on the controller.

191
00:06:09,306 --> 00:06:10,975
I open the controller one,

192
00:06:10,975 --> 00:06:13,029
and the unstashed file is here,

193
00:06:13,029 --> 00:06:15,790
only because the second stage asked for it.

194
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:17,307
One more thing,

195
00:06:17,307 --> 00:06:19,371
the mistake everyone makes once.

196
00:06:19,371 --> 00:06:20,338
A new Pipeline,

197
00:06:20,338 --> 00:06:21,628
named needs windows.

198
00:06:21,628 --> 00:06:23,562
It asks for the label windows.

199
00:06:23,562 --> 00:06:24,852
No machine wears it.

200
00:06:39,402 --> 00:06:40,054
Build Now.

201
00:06:40,054 --> 00:06:41,620
The build does not fail.

202
00:06:41,620 --> 00:06:42,208
It waits.

203
00:06:42,208 --> 00:06:43,317
Open the console.

204
00:06:43,317 --> 00:06:45,339
Still waiting to schedule task.

205
00:06:45,339 --> 00:06:48,080
There are no nodes with the label windows.

206
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:49,450
It will wait forever.

207
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,216
When a build waits,

208
00:06:54,216 --> 00:06:55,368
read this message.

209
00:06:55,368 --> 00:06:56,136
It says why.

210
00:06:56,136 --> 00:06:57,544
Usually a wrong label,

211
00:06:57,544 --> 00:06:59,336
or an agent that is offline.

212
00:06:59,886 --> 00:07:01,545
That is the whole picture.

213
00:07:01,545 --> 00:07:03,077
A controller that plans,

214
00:07:03,077 --> 00:07:04,162
agents that work,

215
00:07:04,162 --> 00:07:05,374
labels that choose,

216
00:07:05,374 --> 00:07:07,353
and files that move on purpose.

217
00:07:08,903 --> 00:07:10,055
Five mistakes.

218
00:07:10,605 --> 00:07:13,062
One: running builds on the controller.

219
00:07:13,062 --> 00:07:15,520
Give it zero executors in a real team,

220
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:16,813
and let agents work.

221
00:07:17,363 --> 00:07:22,675
Two: one executor on a big machine. Match executors to the cores, and to the memory.

222
00:07:23,225 --> 00:07:28,196
Three: a label nobody wears. The build waits forever. Read the console message.

223
00:07:28,746 --> 00:07:32,692
Four: treating the workspace as storage. Archive what you need to keep.

224
00:07:33,242 --> 00:07:35,275
Five: archiving huge folders.

225
00:07:35,275 --> 00:07:37,728
Archive only the files people need,

226
00:07:37,728 --> 00:07:40,602
and stash only what the next stage needs.

227
00:07:42,152 --> 00:07:44,947
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

228
00:07:45,497 --> 00:07:46,961
One: the repository,

229
00:07:46,961 --> 00:07:51,281
GitHub dot com slash it dash waves slash devops-ai,

230
00:07:51,281 --> 00:07:53,625
in the folder academy slash lab.

231
00:07:54,175 --> 00:07:59,807
Two: the files, lab one sixty dot S H, and shortcuts one sixty dot S H.

232
00:08:00,357 --> 00:08:05,818
Three: install it, with sudo install, into slash user slash local slash S bin.

233
00:08:06,368 --> 00:08:08,207
Four: load the short names,

234
00:08:08,207 --> 00:08:10,933
with source shortcuts one sixty dot S H.

235
00:08:10,933 --> 00:08:11,750
Then lab up,

236
00:08:11,750 --> 00:08:12,704
and lab agent.

237
00:08:13,254 --> 00:08:15,750
Five: lab agent creates the agent user,

238
00:08:15,750 --> 00:08:18,374
and prints the one command to connect it.

239
00:08:18,374 --> 00:08:21,190
Lab files writes the three pipeline scripts.

240
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:25,372
Six: you need the Jenkins from lesson one fifty-five,

241
00:08:25,372 --> 00:08:25,989
and Java.

242
00:08:25,989 --> 00:08:29,484
Lab down stops the agent and removes the lab files.

243
00:08:30,034 --> 00:08:31,677
The link is in the description.

244
00:08:33,727 --> 00:08:35,498
Your turn, on your own machine.

245
00:08:36,048 --> 00:08:39,418
One: lab up, then lab agent, and read the command it prints.

246
00:08:39,968 --> 00:08:43,168
Two: add the node in the Jenkins screens, and connect it.

247
00:08:43,718 --> 00:08:47,238
Three: run the agent test, three times, and watch the queue.

248
00:08:47,788 --> 00:08:51,842
Four: run the cloud cart pipeline, and download the archived file.

249
00:08:52,392 --> 00:08:57,640
Five: ask for a label nobody wears, and read the console message. Then lab down.

250
00:08:58,190 --> 00:09:00,024
Pause the video, and begin now.

251
00:09:15,574 --> 00:09:16,449
Quick check.

252
00:09:16,999 --> 00:09:19,815
What is the difference between a controller and an agent?

253
00:09:20,365 --> 00:09:21,666
What is an executor?

254
00:09:22,216 --> 00:09:24,499
When do you archive, and when do you stash?

255
00:09:25,049 --> 00:09:26,713
Why does a build wait forever?

256
00:09:27,263 --> 00:09:29,753
Objective covered: M C seventeen,

257
00:09:29,753 --> 00:09:30,961
objective seven.

258
00:09:30,961 --> 00:09:32,395
Distributed agents,

259
00:09:32,395 --> 00:09:34,281
workspaces and artifacts.

260
00:09:34,831 --> 00:09:36,901
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

261
00:09:47,451 --> 00:09:51,120
Next: approval, promotion, rollback and notifications.

262
00:09:51,670 --> 00:09:54,998
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
